  "Question": "A can of soup can feed \\(3\\) adults or \\(5\\) children. If there are \\(5\\) cans of soup and \\(15\\) children are fed, then how many adults would the remaining soup feed?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "First find how many cans the children use. Since each can feeds \\(5\\) children, feeding \\(15\\) children requires\n\\[15\\div5=3\\text{ cans}.\\]\nThat leaves \\(5-3=2\\) cans. Each remaining can feeds \\(3\\) adults, so the soup can feed \\(2\\cdot3=6\\) adults, choice \\(\\mathrm B\\).",
